note leak fixture (call rule, README.txt): a helper called inside a loop over a public length. The
note caller's registers are spilled to the stack around the BL and loaded back; the slot tracking
note keeps the loop counter and the bound public, so the loop branch stays len after the call.
note The helper's loaded byte reaches only the sum. Expected: TRACE-EQUIV-STATIC PASS.
fn h a view uchar 64 i ulong to ulong
ret ulong get a and i 63
end
fn f a view uchar 64 n ulong to ulong
s = ulong 0
for i ulong n
s = add s h a i
end
ret s
end
